<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#171C1F">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.shopify.com" crossorigin>

    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 48, height: 48 }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Both sides of the "already has the shop name?" test have to be escaped the same way.
      Comparing raw page_title against an escaped shop.name never matches for a name with
      an "&" in it, which is how the home page ended up titled "A&B MOTORS - A&amp;B MOTORS".
      Escaping here also keeps the bare "&" out of the markup.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign shop_name = shop.name | escape_once -%}
    {%- assign head_title = page_title | escape_once -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Compare case-insensitively as well: the SEO title reads "A&B Motors | Used Auto Parts…"
      while shop.name is "A&B MOTORS", and Liquid's `contains` is case-sensitive, so the brand
      was being appended to a title that already led with it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign title_lower = head_title | downcase -%}
    {%- assign shop_lower = shop_name | downcase -%}
    <title>
      {{- head_title -}}
      {%- if current_tags %} &ndash; {{ current_tags | join: ', ' | escape }}{% endif -%}
      {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; Page {{ current_page }}{% endif -%}
      {%- unless title_lower contains shop_lower %} &ndash; {{ shop_name }}{% endunless -%}
    </title>

    {%- comment -%}
      The home page, /collections/all and search have no page_description, so without a
      fallback they shipped no meta description at all — the home page most of all, which
      is the one Google quotes for the business.

      One shared fallback is its own problem, though. Every tag view, every search and
      every paginated page inherited the same shop.description, so a single string was
      repeated across thousands of URLs. Compose from what the page actually is first,
      and fall back to the store description only when there is nothing better to say.

      Tags are checked before page_description on purpose: a tag view of a real
      collection inherits that collection's description, so /collections/wheels and
      /collections/wheels/ford would otherwise ship the identical description.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign listed_count = collections['all'].products_count -%}
    {%- capture listed_count_text -%}
      {%- if listed_count > 0 -%}
        {%- render 'count-with-delimiters', count: listed_count -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign listed_count_text = listed_count_text | strip -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign meta_description = ''

      if request.page_type == 'index' and listed_count_text != blank
        assign meta_description = 'Shop ' | append: listed_count_text | append: ' used OEM auto parts from A&B Motors in Amite, LA. Real photos, 90-day money-back warranty, nationwide shipping, and free local delivery.'
      elsif current_tags.size > 0
        assign tag_list = current_tags | join: ', ' | truncate: 60
        if collection.title != blank and collection.handle != 'all'
          assign meta_description = 'Used ' | append: tag_list | append: ' ' | append: collection.title | append: ' in stock at A&B Motors, Amite LA. Photographed on our own racks, 90-day warranty.'
        else
          assign meta_description = 'Used ' | append: tag_list | append: ' parts in stock at A&B Motors, Amite LA. Pulled, inspected and photographed on our own racks. 90-day warranty.'
        endif
      elsif request.page_type == 'search' and search.performed
        assign meta_description = 'Used OEM parts matching "' | append: search.terms | append: '" at A&B Motors in Amite, LA. Real photos taken at our yard, 90-day warranty, flat-rate shipping shown on every listing.'
      endif

      if meta_description == blank
        assign meta_description = page_description
      endif

      if meta_description == blank and collection.title != blank
        assign meta_description = 'Used ' | append: collection.title | append: ' from A&B Motors in Amite, LA — recycled OEM parts with a 90-day warranty. Flat-rate shipping shown on every listing.'
      endif

      comment
        Shopify has no SEO description field for a policy, and the cart and account pages
        have none either, so all of them fell through to shop.description — the "used auto
        parts, automotive recycling, and used vehicles" blurb, printed identically on the
        Privacy Policy, the Refund Policy and the cart. A page-specific line is worth more
        than a shared one even when the page is not trying to rank.
      endcomment
      if meta_description == blank and request.page_type == 'policy'
        assign meta_description = 'The ' | append: page_title | append: ' for A&B Motors, the used auto parts yard in Amite, Louisiana. Questions? Call 985-748-7195.'
      endif
      if meta_description == blank and request.page_type == 'cart'
        assign meta_description = 'Your cart at A&B Motors. Every part is one of one, so what is held here is the only one we have.'
      endif

      comment
        The last resort used to be shop.description, which is set in Online Store >
        Preferences and reads "...used auto parts, automotive recycling, and used vehicles".
        The yard sells no vehicles and offers no way to shop for one, so every page without
        a description of its own — the blog, 404, account pages, the collection list —
        advertised inventory that does not exist. This says what the site actually is.

        The home page title still says "Used Auto Parts & Vehicles" and shop.description is
        still what it is; both live in Online Store > Preferences, which has no Admin API,
        so neither can be corrected from here.
      endcomment
      assign meta_description = meta_description | default: 'Used OEM auto parts from A&B Motors, a family-run salvage yard in Amite, Louisiana. Real photos, 90-day money-back warranty, nationwide shipping.'

      if current_page != 1
        assign meta_description = meta_description | append: ' Page ' | append: current_page | append: '.'
      endif
    -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      escape_once, not escape: shop.description already stores "&amp;", so escaping it a
      second time shipped "A&amp;amp;B Motors" — which Google would print literally.
      escape_once leaves an existing entity alone and still escapes a bare "&", which is
      what the composed strings above rely on for "A&B Motors".
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if meta_description != blank -%}
      <meta name="description" content="{{ meta_description | strip_html | escape_once }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Indexation policy. Everything here is "follow", never "none": these pages should not
      hold an index entry of their own, but they are how a crawler reaches the products,
      and cutting the link equity with them would cost the listings that do earn one.

      A tag view is the same products behind a filter and a search page is generated on
      demand, so the real collections carry that value.

      Page 2 onward of any paginated list is the same reasoning: /collections/just-pulled
      alone ran to 945 self-canonical pages, and a search engine had already surfaced
      "Just Pulled – Page 386". Page 1 stays indexable and the deep pages stay crawlable.

      Cart and customer account pages are transactional and per-visitor; the cart was
      already appearing in search results.

      A blog with no articles is an H1 and nothing else. This lifts itself the moment
      something is published, so it needs no follow-up.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign no_index = false
      if current_tags.size > 0 or request.page_type == 'search'
        assign no_index = true
      elsif current_page > 1
        assign no_index = true
      elsif request.page_type == 'cart' or request.page_type == 'gift_card'
        assign no_index = true
      elsif request.page_type contains 'customers/'
        assign no_index = true
      elsif request.page_type == 'blog' and blog.articles_count == 0
        assign no_index = true
      endif
    -%}
    {%- if no_index -%}
      <meta name="robots" content="noindex,follow">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Backup verification only. The DNS TXT record on the domain is the real one and
      it keeps working when a different theme is published; this tag does not.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.google_site_verification != blank -%}
      <meta name="google-site-verification" content="{{ settings.google_site_verification | strip | escape }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {% render 'meta-tags', description: meta_description %}

    {{ content_for_header }}

    {% render 'analytics' %}

    {{ 'base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

    {%- liquid
      assign body_font = settings.type_body_font
      assign heading_font = settings.type_heading_font
    -%}
    {% style %}
      {{ body_font | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}
      {{ body_font | font_modify: 'weight', 'bold' | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}
      {{ heading_font | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}
      {{ heading_font | font_modify: 'weight', 'bolder' | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}

      :root {
        --font-body-family: {{ body_font.family }}, {{ body_font.fallback_families }};
        --font-heading-family: {{ heading_font.family }}, {{ heading_font.fallback_families }};
        --green: {{ settings.color_accent }};
        --green-dark: {{ settings.color_accent_dark }};
        --graphite: {{ settings.color_dark }};
        --page: {{ settings.page_width }}px;
      }
    {% endstyle %}

    <script>
      window.ABM = {
        moneyFormat: {{ shop.money_format | json }},
        cartType: {{ settings.cart_type | default: 'stay' | json }},
        routes: {
          cart: {{ routes.cart_url | json }},
          search: {{ routes.search_url | json }},
          predictive: {{ routes.predictive_search_url | json }}
        }
      };
    </script>
    {% render 'shipping-config' %}
    <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
  </head>

  <body class="template-{{ template.name | handle }}"
        {% if template.name == 'product' %}data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"{% endif %}>
    <a class="skip-link btn btn--sm" href="#MainContent">Skip to content</a>

    {% sections 'header-group' %}

    <main id="MainContent" role="main">
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    </main>

    {% sections 'footer-group' %}
  </body>
</html>
